<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bukka Raya I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1377</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Bukka I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bukka Raya I was a co-founder and ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara Empire</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, reigning from about 1356 to 1377 after his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harihara-i">Harihara I</a>. A member of the Sangama family, he extended the kingdom across the south, fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahmani-sultanate">Bahmani Sultanate</a>, and through his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kumara-kampana">Kumara Kampana</a> destroyed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madurai-sultanate">Madurai Sultanate</a>. He also built up the capital, Vijayanagara, on the Tungabhadra river.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bukka-raya-i.jpg" alt="Bukka Raya I" width="320" height="161" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bukkaraya_I_Coin.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
